			<div class="content" id="post-content-4470597">
									

<p>Reviewing this per a request on IRC.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Any changes observed in 5000's condition should be reported to the Department of Tactical Theology immediately.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>In this context, &quot;5000&quot; could refer to the SCP or the outpost.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>towards the approximate direction of Greenland.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I wouldn't describe direction this way. I would use a compass direction.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Those who are currently non-religious, but have been so in the past will typically experience a religious reawakening, professing their return to their faith. Religious personnel transported forcefully to SCP-5000's near proximity will experience seizures and remain incoherent until removed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels incongruous because you had just gotten done talking about religious people, then you jump to former religious people, and then back to religious people again. That order doesn't make sense.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
In general, I find myself not feeling all that strongly about the piece. The fridge logic fell flat for me since I really only know what akiva radiation is in concept and not really much else. All I could really glean was that a god died and the Vatican covered it up by dropping it off in the arctic. It wasn't a satisfying ending, hence my <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">-1</span> novote. The new note helped add some more character to this.
<p><span style="font-size:smaller;"><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> <em>Opinions expressed in this review do not reflect the opinions of SCP Wiki staff as a whole. Please respond to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1581288337" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;">TheMightyMcB</a></span> or contact the captain of the Site Criticism Team, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1581288337" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;">SoullessSingularity</a></span>, for any questions or concerns relating to this review.</em></span></p>

